===== path 
Derive, query, and visualize Toolpath provenance documents

Usage: path [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  show    Show a single session as a markdown summary (used by fzf preview)
  share   Share an agent session to Pathbase via an interactive picker
  resume  Resume an agent session into the chosen harness, projecting the document and exec'ing the harness's resume command
  query   Query the local cache: load every step into one JSON array and transform it with a jaq (jq) filter
  kind    List bundled document kinds, or print a kind's schema (the field reference for `path query`)
  auth    Manage Pathbase credentials for trace uploads
  config  Edit the user configuration (~/.toolpath/config.toml)
  p       Plumbing: lower-level operations on documents and sources (import, export, cache, list, render, merge, validate, derive, project, incept, track, query)
  d       Develop: goldens, record/replay and other tools for working on toolpath itself (built only with the `develop` feature) [aliases: develop]
  haiku   Print a random Toolpath haiku
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
